  "sceneDirections": [
    {
      "sourceLine": 3,
      "title": "Halden loses",
      "direction": "Saturday one, Kiva watching with Aske. Kellan fights well and loses through opponents who learned the shared methods. Conditional sums precede the remaining lanes: Halden cannot now win. Pettit’s heavy hand is support, not a threat. Kiva’s his mother refers to Kellan’s mother, a grader."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 31,
      "title": "The Ropewalk wins",
      "direction": "Saturday two then three. Old Four loses; Ropewalk wins five to three. Carrow borrows and no change, elbows and far edge; she acts on Treen’s call. Lyle’s stance remains, her ward does not return. Kiva traces the method through Pike, Ivey and printed page, without claiming sole invention. Two fingers from Kellan mean the two-mark margin. The crowd may shout in prose; keep Calder controlled."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 71,
      "title": "Thrale arrives",
      "direction": "At ten to five on Saturday, Thrale arrives after a day and a half at sea. Kiva and Mara feel her at forty paces; Kiva’s doors lie down rather than shut. Iron still reports the town count. No voice effect for Glory and no mystical identity change. Thrale is calm but pays physically for this loud town; an hour at a time, lodging outside it at Mole hut. Thirty-six jars are brought, not yet given. Peverell will hear their cost tomorrow. No premature grant or later operation result."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 131,
      "title": "The daily question",
      "direction": "Saturday quarter to seven in the evening, Graving lip rail: yes. Written log is a record, not a new speaker. No later morning hour imported."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 139,
      "title": "The Measure is read",
      "direction": "Ninety-six competitors plus reserves, rows by standing after three boards; Seven still in ninth row. Clerk reads Lane top down, then overall marks bottom up. Keep placements, marks and rows distinct. Tie at sixty-eight goes to Twenty-Eight by first on Hunt; Westerley loses roll place. Seven seventh at sixty-nine, one mark above cutoff: nineteen plus twenty-four plus ten plus sixteen. Its lanes seventeen for, twelve against. No crossing or three doors earned those marks. Ropewalk eighty-two, Halden eighty, two marks apart. Restrained release with awareness of Penhale and displaced four. License is not a warrant; warrant not order; Wednesday response not yet authorized at Saturday reading. No four obliged."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 223,
      "title": "What a license feels like",
      "direction": "Jude records Saturday spend thirty-eight hundredths; three lanes total a dram and eleven, held five and fifteen. Sealed two remains for a hand. He does not yet know what license is worth. Perrin feels the displaced girl’s loss and takes the place anyway; pride in Carry belongs to all names. Pain limits breath without turning narrator into an injured character."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 255,
      "title": "The records arrive",
      "direction": "Saturday nine thirty-five transit. Reader’s brisk custodial care has dry humor without eccentric caricature. Mara receives her sealed page, not Kiva. Annick Personal is under custody and may go back unread; Lumb’s book is borrowed. Wax and figures across join preserve provenance, not truth of an interpretation. Tomorrow’s reading has not occurred."
    },
    {
      "sourceLine": 283,
      "title": "Anwen chooses her place",
      "direction": "Saturday quarter past ten, Kiva hears first. Anwen already signed yes: own place on Mace’s line, two nights a week and Hall otherwise, reduced future Seven lanes. Going somewhere is not abandonment. Sharing wall method with opponents is the work’s purpose. Kiva is glad and will miss her, both. Brief embrace, no sentimental swell. Nine at Counting House precedes two at Graving tomorrow."
    }
  ],
